danu (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * danu-build collected its run log with journalctl -u dem-build, the unit
    name from before the move, so every published log since the cutover was
    empty. The build itself was unaffected.
  * Declare python3-pyosmium and zip. The contour output and square recovery
    import osmium, and three scripts call zip; neither was in Depends, and the
    only machine running this had pyosmium installed by hand years ago.
  * The published log and progress files are danu-build-log*.txt and
    danu-build-progress.txt, matching what the elevation guide already said.
  * The pure geometry and grading move to danu.core.profile, which imports no
    GDAL, so the tests run on Windows and the duplication between
    danu.checks.rivers and danu.water.constraints is gone.

 -- Lee Kindness <wangi@opengeofiction.net>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0000

danu (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First package. The elevation pipeline moved out of ogf-server-scripts,
    restructured into the danu packages, with the systemd units renamed from
    dem-build and backup-elevation to danu-build and danu-backup.

 -- OpenGeofiction administrators <admin@opengeofiction.net>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0000
